3. Constitution of Pakistan Tea Board.___(1) As soon as may be, the Federal Government shall constitute a body to be called the Pakistan Tea Board consisting of the following members, that is to say:___

(a) A Chairman to be appointed by the Federal Government ;

(aa) three members elected by the Pakistan Tea Association * * *;

(b) two members elected by the Tea Traders Association of Pakistan of whom one shall represent the tea brokers and shippers and the other the tea traders;

(c) one member to be nominated by the Federal Government to represent the estates under proprietary management;

*

*

*

* * * *
(e) two persons possessing special knowledge of tea or tea cultivation, or agriculture, to be nominated by the Federal Government ;

(f) one person to be elected by the recognized labour unions of tea gardens;

(g) one officer serving under the Federal Government in the Ministry of Commerce to be nominated by the Federal Government.

(2) The Federal Government shall publish in the official Gazette the names of all the members of the Board and thereupon the Board shall be deemed to be constituted.

(3) Members of the Board shall, subject to the provisions of sub-section (4), hold office for three years, and shall be eligible for re-election or re-nomination.

1Ins. ibid.

1Subs. by F.A.O., 1975, Art. 2 and Table, for “Central Government”.
